"description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T04:22:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia clinches SEC title game berth with win at South Carolina","description":"Nate Frazier ran for 94 yards and two touchdowns, and No. 1 Georgia clinched a spot in the final SEC championship game with a victory over South Carolina on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T05:47:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50558713/georgia-clinches-sec-title-game-berth-win-south-carolina","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios for Week 12?","description":"Here's what teams from every conference would need to play for their league championship.","published":"2026-11-22T04:00:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Miami tops Virginia Tech, to face Wake Forest in ACC title game","description":"Miami will play Wake Forest in the ACC title game on Dec. 5 after both teams won on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T04:46:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50558418/miami-tops-virginia-tech-face-wake-forest-acc-title-game","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Betting buzz: Big Ten's odds of national champion four-peat getting slim","description":"Losses by UCLA, Indiana and Ohio State make the Big Ten's chances of winning the national championship this season a long shot.","published":"2026-11-22T04:06:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/49921234/college-football-betting-buzz-odds-updates-line-moves-spreads","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Emotional Greg Schiano authors 'special' win, Rutgers' first at PSU since 1988","description":"Less than two weeks after Rutgers announced embattled Greg Schiano would return as coach for a 19th season, the Scarlet Knights stunned Penn State 25-24 on Saturday, their first win over the Nittany Lions since 1988, and just their third this year.","published":"2026-11-22T02:56:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50557643/rutgers-authors-special-win-1st-penn-state-1988","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922981/rasheem-biles","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Rasheem Biles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:23Z","intro":"Rasheem Biles (born November 18, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Texas Longhorns. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Biles attended Pickerington High School Central in Pickerington, Ohio, where he played wide receiver, running back and defensive back. As a senior he played in five games due to injury and had over 400 all-purpose yards and five total touchdowns including two interceptions returned for touchdown. As a junior he had 74 tackles and three interceptions with two returned for a touchdown. Biles committed to the University of Pittsburgh to play college."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"PITTSBURGH\nAs a true freshman at Pittsburgh in 2023, Biles played in nine games and tied a school record with three blocked punts. He became a starter his sophomore year in 2024, starting nine of 12 games and recording 82 tackles, 5.5 sacks and an interception which he returned for a touchdown. He returned to Pittsburgh as a starter in 2025, playing in 10 games and recording 101 tackles, 4.5 sacks, two interceptions, both returned for touchdowns, two forced fumbles, and one fumble recovery, returned for a touchdown. At the end of the season, Biles entered the transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS\nOn January 10, 2026, Biles committed to Texas. In Week 9 against Mississippi State, Biles recorded eight tackles, including three sacks and four tackles for a loss, and two forced fumbles, earning SEC Co-Defensive Player of the Week for his performance."}]}}